{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I want a file named color.txt in the project. Before you create it, ask me which color I prefer, red or blue. If you have a tool that puts a question to me directly, use it. Wait for my answer, then write exactly my answer into color.txt and reply with one short sentence naming the color.","cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}}]}],"max_tokens":128000,"stream":true,"system":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n- tool_search: Search for tools that are not loaded yet and load the matches\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\n/work/project\n</cwd>\n\n<t3_code_orchestration>\n## T3 Code orchestration\n\nOrdinary coding tasks need no T3 tools.\n\n- Subagents: use your native tool when the child uses your provider, a model it offers and no settings beyond yours (Claude `Agent`, `run_in_background:false`; Codex `spawn_agent`, then wait). Use `delegate_task` for another provider's model, user-asked settings, a separate checkout (`isolation:\"worktree\"`), or `delegate_task` by name. A native type on another provider's model counts too. Background agent: `delegate_task`, never a background `Agent`. Workflow only when asked.\n- Call `orchestrator_capabilities` once per thread, before the first `delegate_task`. Again only after an error or a user-named provider change. Settings go in `target.options`. Provider or model unavailable: say so. Never switch unasked or fall back to native tools, Workflow or CLIs. Never make a child's checkout in the shell or in `task`.\n- Every new delegate review or re-check is a new `delegate_task` (brief, findings, objections), never a `t3_thread_send`. Fix small review findings yourself; start no delegate for them. When told to proceed without a delegate, or to run fewer, `task_cancel` the extras. Start no replacement.\n- Follow a running delegate's `next`. Don't poll it (`task_status`, `sleep`, watchers, Monitor, ScheduleWakeup). Stop a delegate run you replace or no longer need with `task_cancel`, never `t3_thread_interrupt` on a `childThreadId`.\n- As a subagent or child, do the work yourself. Start no subagents unless your task says to.\n\n- `t3_thread_launch` and `create_threads` make new top-level threads, only when the user asks for a new thread. \"Subagent\", \"delegate\", and \"parallel\" never mean one. Worktree thread: set `workspaceStrategy`. Honor a requested base. Otherwise independent work uses the default branch as `remote/branch` with `startFromOrigin:true`; with no remote, use the local default. Required unpublished commits and dependent work use their local base. Shell worktrees don't bind it, and no checkout setup in its prompt. No `workspaceStrategy`: project root, not your worktree.\n- Given a thread id, `t3_thread_read` it before you answer about it. Asked to settle a thread, this one too: `t3_thread_organize`.\n- Another machine: `t3_environment_links` lists linked ones. Pass its `environmentId` and that machine's `threadId` to T3 tools.\n- Unlinked (\"delegate this to my vps\"): `t3_environment_link` with a `hint` from the user's words, never a pairing code in chat. No link tools: say to enable Settings → Labs → Linked environments.\n- In your reply, mention a thread by its `link`, verbatim, never a plain title or bare id.\n- A login, token, PIN, pairing code or sudo password only the user can give: call `request_secret`, not a chat ask or a handoff. Not for access you have. Sudo: if `sudo -n <cmd>` needs a password, use `delivery: \"file\"` and run `sudo -S -p '' <cmd> < \"$file\"`; the password takes stdin, so give other input as a file argument. Asked only to schedule: `schedule_task` without running its prompt.\n- T3 tools may load late. Try the name once before you call it absent.\n\n### Visuals and preview\n\n- Answer data with a trend or comparison with a chart and show any visual the user asks for here: pass an HTML file path or inline HTML to `html_preview`, then `html_render`. A screenshot on disk or a text description doesn't show it. Never start a server for it. Page tools write only on user request. Never use them to show results. Asked for an image to post, send or use elsewhere: a `.png` file and its path, never `html_render`.\n- Never use `preview_*` unasked to verify or show your own edit. Use them when the current request asks for browser work, including recording edits, or names a page or tab. Don't repeat preview calls from an earlier turn. Public pages: web fetch or search unless browser work was asked; then preview tools only, no web fetch. Close a tab you opened before you reply, unless the user asked for it or uses it.\n\n<pull_request_linking>\nLink each PR you create, take over, or push to: link_pull_request, or link_pull_requests for several, full URL, every stack layer, as your next call. Host tools don't link for you. If linking fails, say so. Skip PRs you only read or review and PRs named only as background. Call watch_pull_request when asked to monitor or babysit, or when work you were asked to do, such as a merge, still waits on checks or reviews, even after an earlier unwatch. Finish any needed branch update and push first, then watch and end your turn. Otherwise act now or hand back. Delegated children never watch, even if the brief says babysit. After PR work, a child's last line is: PR <full URL>, head <SHA>, checks and reviews <state>. Links and watches persist across pushes. For PR waits, no sleep, loops, gh --watch, Monitor or ScheduleWakeup. Before handback, call unwatch_pull_request on any PR you watch. When pull_request_* tools are listed, use them, not gh or cafe, to read, list, open, edit, review, reply on, close, or merge PRs, and ci_logs and ci_rerun for their checks. pull_request_create links for you.\nIf available, call link_issue for each issue you take on or file, even via CLI; skip issues you only read.\n</pull_request_linking>\n</t3_code_orchestration>","cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}}],"tools":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","eager_input_streaming":true,"strict":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","required":["path","offset","limit"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","eager_input_streaming":true,"strict":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","required":["command","timeout"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","eager_input_streaming":true,"strict":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","eager_input_streaming":true,"strict":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}},"additionalProperties":false}},{"name":"mcp__t3-code__orchestrator_capabilities","description":"List providers, models, options, and runtime modes for `delegate_task`. Short list. `search` finds others. Any catalog model works.","eager_input_streaming":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"environmentId":{"type":"string"},"search":{"type":"string"}},"required":[]}},{"name":"mcp__t3-code__delegate_task","description":"Start one child agent with only `task`. No parent history. Separate checkout or PR per child: `isolation:'worktree'`. Keep `taskId` for `task_status` and `task_cancel`. No secrets in `task`.","eager_input_streaming":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"task":{"type":"string"},"target":{"type":"object","properties":{"providerInstanceId":{"type":"string"},"driverKind":{"type":"string"},"model":{"type":"string"},"options":{"description":"Options from `orchestrator_capabilities`, such as {effort:'max'}. Given values override inherited. [] or {} clears.","anyOf":[{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"value":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"boolean"}]}},"required":["id","value"]}},{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"boolean"}]}}]},"environmentId":{"type":"string"},"projectId":{"type":"string"}}},"title":{"type":"string"},"role":{"type":"string","enum":["implementation","research","review","design","test","general"]},"isolation":{"type":"string","enum":["shared","worktree"],"description":"'shared' (default): parent checkout. 'worktree': new prepared checkout from the parent commit, for a separate checkout or PR per child. Uncommitted edits stay out."},"mode":{"type":"string","enum":["async","wait"],"description":"Default 'async'. 'wait' only if this turn needs the result. A question or approval ends the wait."},"timeoutMs":{"type":"number","description":"Mode 'wait' only. At most 45 s. A timeout does not cancel the child."},"clientRequestId":{"type":"string"},"runtimeMode":{"type":"string","enum":["inherit","approval-required","auto-accept-edits","auto","full-access"],"description":"Omit unless the user asks for a supervised child. Narrow modes pause for human approval, not read-only. Above yours is rejected."},"interactionMode":{"type":"string","enum":["inherit","default","plan"]}},"required":["task"]}},{"name":"mcp__t3-code__task_status","description":"Read one delegated task you started. Do not call it on a running task before its completion wakes you. `workState`: working, waiting_for_children, result_available. A finished turn with live child work is not done. `summary`: final result. Reading it marks it delivered.","eager_input_streaming":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"taskId":{"type":"string"}},"required":["taskId"]}},{"name":"ask_user","description":"Ask the user a question and wait for the reply. Pass options when the reply is a choice between known values.","eager_input_streaming":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"question":{"type":"string","description":"The question to show the user"},"options":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Choices to offer"}},"required":["question"]}},{"name":"tool_search","description":"# Tool discovery\n\nSearches over deferred tool metadata with BM25 and exposes matching tools for the next model call.\n\nSome of the tools, such as tools of MCP servers, may not have been provided to you upfront, and you should use this tool (`tool_search`) to search for the required tools. For MCP tool discovery, always use `tool_search`.","eager_input_streaming":true,"input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","description":"Search query for deferred tools."},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of tools to return. Defaults to 8."}},"required":["query"]},"cache_control":{"type":"ephemeral"}},{"name":"__pi_deferred_placeholder__","description":"Reserved placeholder. Never available. Never call this.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"defer_loading":true}],"thinking":{"type":"disabled"},"thread":{"type":"create"}}